From: Louis Maliyam <louis@nexthop.ai>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dts: bindings: aspeed,ast27xx-sdrammc: add max-dram-size-mb

Let a board cap the DRAM capacity that the AST2700 BootMCU detects. The
wrap-around size probe can over-report the capacity: a 4 GiB DDR5 x16
part on Nexthop's AST2720-A2 BMC card is detected as 8 GiB on cold boot.

Signed-off-by: Louis Maliyam <louis@nexthop.ai>
---
diff --git a/dts/bindings/riscv/aspeed,ast27xx-sdrammc.yaml b/dts/bindings/riscv/aspeed,ast27xx-sdrammc.yaml
index 0594e8b..c6e3122 100644
--- a/dts/bindings/riscv/aspeed,ast27xx-sdrammc.yaml
+++ b/dts/bindings/riscv/aspeed,ast27xx-sdrammc.yaml
@@ -27,3 +27,11 @@ properties:
     type: int
     required: false
     description: Size of AES encryption in bytes
+  max-dram-size-mb:
+    type: int
+    required: false
+    description: |
+      Upper bound of the DRAM capacity in MiB (256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096
+      or 8192). The wrap-around size probe result is clamped to this
+      value. Use it when the fitted part is known and the probe can
+      over-report the capacity.
